1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,344
So, what should you do if your cashless is denied at the counter tonight?

2
00:00:04,344 --> 00:00:06,495
Do not shout at hospital staff.

3
00:00:06,495 --> 00:00:08,048
Do not panic.

4
00:00:08,048 --> 00:00:09,840
Follow these four steps.

5
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:10,863
Step One.

6
00:00:10,863 --> 00:00:13,021
Collect your papers before you leave.

7
00:00:13,021 --> 00:00:15,560
If you have to pay the bill yourself, pay it.

8
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:26,169
But before leaving the hospital, ask for copies of the discharge summary, the final itemized bill, all test reports, pharmacy receipts, and the written cashless denial letter.

9
00:00:26,169 --> 00:00:32,880
If they claimed admission was not needed, ask your treating doctor for a short clinical justification certificate.

10
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:33,864
Step Two.

11
00:00:33,864 --> 00:00:37,744
File for reimbursement within fifteen to thirty days of discharge.

12
00:00:37,744 --> 00:00:40,047
Check your policy for your exact limit.

13
00:00:40,047 --> 00:00:45,760
If they reject it, write a calm, formal email to the company's Grievance Redressal Officer.

14
00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:55,111
State your policy number, claim number and amount, and if your policy has crossed five years, quote the I-R-D-A-I five-year moratorium rule.

15
00:00:55,111 --> 00:00:58,042
The company must reply within fourteen days.

16
00:00:58,042 --> 00:00:59,094
Step Three.

17
00:00:59,094 --> 00:01:01,217
Register on Bima Bharosa.

18
00:01:01,217 --> 00:01:09,545
If the company ignores you or sends the same generic rejection, go to Bima Bharosa dot I-R-D-A-I dot gov dot in.

19
00:01:09,545 --> 00:01:15,675
This is the regulator's own portal, and complaints filed here are tracked directly by the I-R-D-A-I.

20
00:01:15,675 --> 00:01:16,794
And Step Four.

21
00:01:16,794 --> 00:01:18,660
The Insurance Ombudsman.

22
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:28,302
If the company still refuses after thirty days, you do NOT need a consumer court case, and you do NOT need an expensive lawyer.

23
00:01:28,302 --> 00:01:31,450
Go to the official website, c-i-o-i-n-s dot co dot in.

24
00:01:31,450 --> 00:01:36,929
The Insurance Ombudsman is a government body set up specifically to resolve insurance disputes.

25
00:01:36,929 --> 00:01:38,207
You can file online.

26
00:01:38,207 --> 00:01:39,956
It costs zero rupees.

27
00:01:39,956 --> 00:01:41,615
You do not need a lawyer.

28
00:01:41,615 --> 00:01:49,310
In the financial year twenty twenty-four to twenty-five, the Ombudsman offices received over thirty-two thousand health complaints.

29
00:01:49,310 --> 00:01:55,456
Of the cases they settled or decided, over seventy-five percent went in favor of the policyholder.

30
00:01:55,456 --> 00:01:59,158
And eight out of ten complaints were closed within three months.

31
00:01:59,158 --> 00:02:05,945
The Ombudsman can award up to fifty lakh rupees, and the award is legally binding on the insurance company.

32
00:02:05,945 --> 00:02:09,828
Finally... how do you prevent this before you even buy?

33
00:02:09,828 --> 00:02:10,744
Rule One.

34
00:02:10,744 --> 00:02:13,925
Disclose everything in writing on the proposal form.

35
00:02:13,925 --> 00:02:17,596
If you smoke or take mild B-P medication, declare it.

36
00:02:17,596 --> 00:02:21,071
Once it's on paper, they can never call it non-disclosure.

37
00:02:21,071 --> 00:02:22,027
Rule Two.

38
00:02:22,027 --> 00:02:24,771
Choose a policy with No Room Rent Capping.

39
00:02:24,771 --> 00:02:30,713
In our example, one bigger room cost almost sixty thousand rupees through proportionate cuts.

40
00:02:30,713 --> 00:02:31,727
Rule Three.

41
00:02:31,727 --> 00:02:33,980
Ask about a Consumables Cover.

42
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:39,846
Reports say gloves, masks, and syringes can be five to fifteen percent of a hospital bill.

43
00:02:39,846 --> 00:02:42,735
Some insurers sell an add-on cover for this.

44
00:02:42,735 --> 00:02:45,569
Check its price and its limit before you buy.

45
00:02:45,569 --> 00:02:50,454
Remember, you pay for insurance so your family has peace of mind.

46
00:02:50,454 --> 00:02:52,060
Know the five-year rule.

47
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:53,331
Use the Ombudsman.

48
00:02:53,331 --> 00:02:55,727
And protect your hard-earned savings.

49
00:02:55,727 --> 00:02:56,604
Be smart.

50
00:02:56,604 --> 00:02:57,676
Be informed.

51
00:02:57,676 --> 00:02:59,997
And always... be practical.

52
00:02:59,997 --> 00:03:07,602
If this helped you, share it with a family member who has health insurance, subscribe to Be Practical with Kishore, and ask your questions below.

53
00:03:07,602 --> 00:03:08,604
I'll see you next time.

